  This is the current `master` branch source, NOT the stale npm
  package `epubjs@0.3.93` (published 2022-02-16). The npm tag has not
  been updated since; this build was produced directly from the
  GitHub source tree instead.

BUILD
  Command:  NODE_ENV=production MINIMIZE=true webpack --progress
            (NODE_OPTIONS=--openssl-legacy-provider required — this
            webpack/babel toolchain predates Node's OpenSSL 3 provider
            change and fails without it on current Node.)
  Modification from upstream: upstream's webpack.config.js declares
  `externals: { "jszip/dist/jszip": "JSZip", "xmldom": "xmldom" }`,
  which produces a build that expects a separately-loaded global
  `window.JSZip` at runtime. That externals block was removed for
  this build so jszip and xmldom are compiled directly into
  epub.min.js, producing one self-contained file — matching this
  project's existing js/vendor/pdfjs/ convention (a single vendored
  script, no second file to load, no external global to wire up).
  This is the only change made to upstream's build configuration;
  no application source in src/ was modified.

